clang: the EmiBSD toolchain driver

Why a patch: the driver must know how the system links and what it defaults to.
ToolChains/EmiBSD.{h,cpp} (new, ISC) are the toolchain: PIE by default, rcrt0.o
for a static PIE (-static, or -static-pie as rustc asks), gcrt0.o for -pg, crtbegin/crtend from the sysroot's /usr/lib,
the entry __start, --eh-frame-hdr, /usr/libexec/ld.so, lld, compiler-rt's
builtins before and after -lc, libc++ with libc++abi (which carries the
unwinder, D-0010), the strong
stack protector, asynchronous unwind tables, /usr/include of the sysroot and nothing
else for C; for C++, libc++'s headers where clang's generic search finds them (the
toolchain's include/<triple>/c++/v1 and include/c++/v1, else the sysroot's
/usr/include/c++/v1). The tables of the shared driver code learn the
OS: toolchain selection, the OS library name `emibsd`, no GCC include tree, PIE
level 1 (-fpie), no -lrt and no -ldl (the libc has both), -p allowed, and the
hardening defaults the system's libraries are built with: on AArch64 branch
target enforcement and return address signing, on x86-64 IBT.
Written by EmiBSD (ISC); carried by DevTools over the pinned tag. Author: Emilio
Navarrete Lineros, 2026-10-31.

